<title>PHILIPPINES: PAL stockholders agree to double capital.</title>
<headline>PAL stockholders agree to double capital.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Airlines' stockholders voted at a meeting on Tuesday to double the carrier's authorised capital to 10 billion pesos from the current 5.0 billion pesos, company officials said.  </p>
<p>Current stockholders will be given 14 days to subscribe to the additional capital, the officials told reporters after the shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>The increase in capital will enable the loss-making airline to press ahead with a $4 billion re-fleeting programme, they said.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-8936</p>
